In $\Om$, we have $\curlvec \tilde{\E}_p=\curlvec \E_p$. Moreover, in $\Pi_x$ we find
\[
\curlvec \E_p=\curlvec \left(\begin{array}{c}
0\\
E_y\\
E_z
\end{array}\right)=\left(\begin{array}{c}
\partial_yE_z-\partial_zE_y\\
-\partial_xE_z\\
\partial_xE_y
\end{array}\right).
\]
