	\begin{prop}\label{Feb_23_2024_2} $(\Cun,\leq)$ has the $n$-amalgamation property for every $n$.  In fact, if $A\leq B$ and $n<\omega$ are given, we can always take $m= n+|B\smallsetminus A|$.
